  "python": {
    "sha256": "b2999362f6dfaf47a9f50ffd41a73f7c710bf875f21e85159cda931766908a3c",
    "descriptions": [
      {
        "path": [
          "description"
        ],
        "key": "schema.tool.7a311a1aca572342",
        "present": true,
        "source": "Run Python directly, without shell quoting. h is already praxis_hands: h.read, h.edit, h.write, h.search use the same editor, version checks and receipts. h.hand('name', **args) calls any hand in this turn's authorized catalogue through the live parent dispatcher, with its rights, durable receipts and Stop. r['outcome'] is the hand's own outcome (confirmed/refused/in_doubt/partial/ok/failed, unknown if it reports none); print r['content'] for its reply; r also has result_ref, call_id and image_count. h.describe('name')['content'] gives the full schema. InDoubt means check the receipt, never repeat the effect blindly. The bridge expires when this outer call returns or reaches its ceiling; a nested hand already started when the script stops waiting still finishes and its receipt follows [exit N]. Standalone workers/background survivors have no live bridge. Print results you need. cwd defaults to your local home, or the local Forge task root with task_id. Local task execution inherits custody and Stop; remote tasks are refused before execution. At home timeout=0 uses the configured shell default (normally 30s), capped at 600s; in a task 0 means unlimited. The output ends with [exit N]; a timeout closes the ordinary process group. Background descendants survive normal completion. Prefer h.edit to whole-file string replacement. To run one program with exact arguments, call run_command instead of subprocess glue."
